{% doc %}
  Writes a delivery line with the free shipping threshold filled in.

  The threshold used to be typed into five separate pieces of copy — the bag,
  the shop page's line, two delivery notes and the policy text — so raising it
  meant remembering all five, and forgetting one left the site promising two
  different things. Now it is one number in theme settings and every sentence
  writes itself from it.

  Write [free_over] wherever the amount belongs.

  @param {string} text - The sentence, with or without the placeholder.

  @example
  {% render 'brand-delivery-text', text: section.settings.terms %}
{% enddoc %}

{%- comment -%}
  Without trailing zeros, so a round threshold reads as "200 SAR" the way the
  copy was written rather than "200.00". The currency and its position still
  come from the store's own money format.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign free_over = settings.free_shipping_threshold | times: 100 | money_without_trailing_zeros -%}
{{- text | replace: '[free_over]', free_over -}}
